# NOTES #

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hominidae#cite_ref-5]  "Great ape" is a common name rather than a taxonomic label, and there are differences in usage, even by the same author. The term may or may not include humans, as when Dawkins writes "Long before people thought in terms of evolution ... great apes were often confused with humans" [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hominidae#cite_note-3] [ [LINK: (better source needed) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Verifiability#Questionable_sources] ] and "gibbons are faithfully monogamous, unlike the great apes which are our closer relatives." [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hominidae#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDawkins2005126-4] [ [LINK: (better source needed) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Verifiability#Questionable_sources] ]


